meta {
  name: stacks: from template
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/stacks/from-template
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "template": "{{template_id}}:queue-v1",
    "stack_id": "{{stack_id}}",
    "pod_ids": {
      "main": "{{stack_id}}"
    },
    "secrets": {},
    "overrides": {
      "worker": { "resources": { "cpu_limit": 1000, "mem_limit": 2048 } }
    },
    "description": "my n8n"
  }
}

docs {
  ## Instantiate a whole stack in one call (PROPOSED — Part D, not yet implemented)
  
  Expands the `kind=stack` template into a Stack + its member pods. With `stack_id = myn8n`:
  
  | member | resolved pod_id | why |
  |---|---|---|
  | db     | `myn8ndb`     | derived `{stack_id}{name}` |
  | redis  | `myn8nredis`  | derived |
  | main   | `myn8n`       | **overridden** via `pod_ids` → clean public URL `myn8n.pods.<base>` |
  | worker | `myn8nworker` | derived |
  
  - **`pod_ids`** — per-member override of the public id (precedence: this > member's template
    `pod_id` > `{stack_id}{name}`). Rename only the pods that matter (the frontend); the rest stay
    prefixed and collision-free.
  - **`secrets`** — fill any *required* placeholder secrets the template declared. Empty here
    because `PG_PASSWORD`/`N8N_ENC_KEY` are `${pods:random:N}` (generated once, shared).
  - **`overrides`** — per-member field overrides applied on top of the template (here, smaller
    worker limits).
  - **Cross-member refs resolve to literals**: `${stack:db:host}` → `pods-<site>-<tenant>-myn8ndb`;
    `${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}` → the one generated password.
  - **Atomic**: the whole set is validated up front (names, id charset/length/uniqueness, no
    cycles, `ready`⇒probe); if any member fails to create, everything already created is rolled back.
}
